{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/28630-wraiths-and-lifesight","id":28630,"title":"Wraiths and Lifesight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-12T04:35:36-08:00","id":28630,"title":"Wraiths and Lifesight","content":"Playing a Wraith for the first time, and while trying to find info for more detail on Life/Death sight, I found this<br /> <br /> - <u>Spirit Sense</u> The spirits and denizens of the Middle Umbra make slight impressions on the fabric of the Shadowlands that are even further dampened by the Shroud, so few wraiths are even aware of the potential for this application of Lifesight. Only wraiths with a considerable knowledge of Garou and their relation to the Umbra can attempt this. The wraith can vaguely detect the presence of the Umbral entities, such as Garou, spirits, and banes with a roll of Perception + Occult (difficulty equal to the local Shroud + 2, but no greater than 10). It should be noted that this requires concentration, and therefore isn't something that someone completely ignorant of werewolf cosmology would &quot;accidentally&quot; notice.<br /> <br /> Does anybody have any sort of a source on this? Or any other information about Wraiths mucking with spirits in other portions of the Umbra?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1645-autochthon","name":"Autochthon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T04:59:09-08:00","id":28638,"title":"","content":"I think this was in the companion book like Dead Secrets.<br /> <br /> Wraiths have little truck with the Spirits of the Umbra, but some have wound up there such as the Lost Legion that got blasted by the Maelstrom into the Abyss. It would be cool to someday get some sort of Animistic Arcanos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T14:46:42-08:00","id":29542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/28630-wraiths-and-lifesight?p=28638#post28638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this was in the companion book like Dead Secrets.<br /> <br /> Wraiths have little truck with the Spirits of the Umbra, but some have wound up there such as the Lost Legion that got blasted by the Maelstrom into the Abyss. It would be cool to someday get some sort of Animistic Arcanos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there was also some talk that in the old prime age (when mages didn't have paradox, the shapechangers were blah blah, and enoch was in this world) there were no tares so to speak. The umbral and shadow and regular worlds were all merged together and not seperated by spirit walls. So if some ghost is that old (we'er talking antedeluv or archmage sphere 9 kind of old here) they may remember that and be able to teach this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T14:07:32-08:00","id":331466,"title":"","content":"I recall that the different uses for Life/Death Sight were listed in the Wraith Player's Guide (a 1st edition release); I believe the Spirit Sense rule was first presented there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is the Line of Division...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3797-terminus-est","name":"Terminus Est","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3797_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T02:05:33-08:00","id":332064,"title":"","content":"I honestly can't say what utility a Wraith is going to get out of that ability, considering that they don't really have any means of interacting with the Middle Umbra. Maybe if a wraith got their hands on an artifact that allowed it, they could interact with spirits in some fashion.<br /> <br /> If I recall correctly, we never did get a book for the Proctors guild... perhaps that book might have contained arts to use Embody to travel to the middle umbra? I suppose we will never know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T10:56:20-08:00","id":333218,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I can't really think of any Artifacts or Arcanoi that would allow a wraith to crossover from the Underworld into the Umbra. About the only way to get from one to the other I can think of, that would be useable to a wraith, is to get to the Dark Kingdom of Jade, make it across the Ebon Road into the 1000 Hells, find the Scarlet Path and cross it into the Umbra. That's about as treacherous journey as one could take. Hell it makes being a Doomslayer look like a pleasant summer stroll in a park.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}